      $VER: FPSubboardActivityGraph, v1.00 (30-Jun-96) by Dotoran!
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

Disclaimer:
~~~~~~~~~~
    Originally, v.30 was written by PMK, aka Peter Klein. Since Peter has
decided to go the IBM route, I'll be attempting to "take on" the continued
development of the files he has authored in the past.

What Is It?
~~~~~~~~~~
    This mod creates a bar graph showing the usage of the different subboards
on your bbs. The user can specify if they wish to view the usage of the Base
subboards(Message Bases), the UDBase subboards(File Bases), or a Mixture of
both.

    The graph will show a percentage usage in each area, as well as the total
number of NEW items placed in that subboard, since FPSAG's last reset. The
bars will be labeled B or U if the user chooses Mixture, so they'll know if
the base in question is a Message or File subboard.

    The SysOp (or any user with the "System Operator" priviledge flag set)
will also see an option to RESET the FPSAG, upon which the reset date will
be updated to the current date, and all data files will be deleted.

How Do I Install It?
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1. Copy the "FPSAG/" directory into your "FPFiles/" directory, if you have
   one, or else copy the "FPFiles/FPSAG/" directory somewhere on your bbs
   system.

   NOTE: All files in the Dotoran released "FP" series reside in the parent
         "FPFiles/" directory, so as to keep them grouped together. It is
         highly recommended you do the same.

2. Load your BBSTEXT file into an editor, then add the following command to
   the beginning of lines 791 and 816:

            {#0<path>FPFiles/FPSAG/FPSAGUP}
            ^
        Control-Q

   NOTE: Replace <path> above with the path you stored the directory during
         Step # 1 above.

3. Now load your BBSMENU file into the editor and add the following line to
   Menu # 2; Available Everywhere:

            FPSAG       `3-  |  {#0<path>FPFiles/FPSAG/FPSAG}
                        ^       ^
                   Groups       Control-Q

   NOTE: Again, replace <path> using the same path as in Step # 1 above.

4. You can modify a couple variables located in the "FPSAG" command file to
   set colors, max number of bases to display, etc.

5. That's It! Reload your BBSTEXT and BBSMENU files and you're ready to
   start using this mod.

NOTE: The graph will appear BLANK when you first look at it, as it needs
      to create data files for each base, as they start being used on your
      bbs. Each time a base is entered, it's data is updated. Go about your
      regular bbs usage for a day or so, then try the FPSAG command. You'll
      be shown the bases that have received usage within that time. (If you
      simplay cannot wait, just go into each base, as that will create the
      needed file inside the "FPSAG/FPSAGd/" directory! hehe)
